    "unverified_targets": {
      "cursor": "Event beforeShellExecution, input field command, answer fields permission, user_message and agent_message, and the failClosed option come from a snapshot of Cursor's hook page in a local outside project and match Cursor's hook page as read on September 24, 2026, which requires permission in every answer and blocks the action on an answer that does not match the schema. So an allowed command is answered with permission allow. No Cursor run was observed. Whether Cursor then still asks the user under its own approval settings is unverified; if it does not, this allowlist is the only approval for shell commands in Cursor.",
      "copilot": "Event preToolUse, input fields toolName and toolArgs, the permissionDecision and permissionDecisionReason answer, the empty answer that keeps the default behavior, and the version, bash, cwd and timeoutSec keys match GitHub's hooks configuration reference as read on September 24, 2026; no Copilot run was observed."
    },
